{"id": "EUVD-2026-55569", "enisaUuid": "0957d372-4937-3b40-a5c9-b133b1ae4930", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/guc: Keep scheduler timeline name alive\n\nThe scheduler keeps a pointer to the timeline name, but q->name\nis freed with the exec queue while scheduler fences can still\nreference it.\n\nStore the name in struct xe_guc_exec_queue so it shares\nthe scheduler's RCU-deferred lifetime.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 41075f0eb5dcbd3b065d15f15ef7bbe9315188e8)", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:04:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:54", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eac2839585741e6c1b4af261a0b58bca0d6f5436", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88c38ff74f8345fcf8852549f94025754019b037", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77fd62412431e8c80ef2ad61466bc76fe425f80a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/299bc6d50b1bed7d1f408391736712f01a0855e2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hf5h-j5wg-pf5g", "CVE-2026-68383"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05644da5-ee29-37ed-8f02-570ff37837dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16.2 <6.17"}, {"id": "0d85b9f2-bba6-302d-8346-802007c01228", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6bd90e700b4285e6a7541e00f969cab0d696adde <299bc6d50b1bed7d1f408391736712f01a0855e2"}, {"id": "23427a66-165e-3732-be77-1b7518e1cb99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "30a32c48-24a7-389c-a015-12def54a1176", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "683b0e397dad9f26a42dcacf6f7f545a77ce6c06"}, {"id": "5f1928e5-f915-332e-b7ca-bf44b816cd64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b17fcce70733c211cb5dabf54f4f9491920b1d92 <eac2839585741e6c1b4af